Package: tower-tray
Version: @VERSION@
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Maintainer: @MAINTAINER@
Depends: tower (= @VERSION@), python3-gi, python3-gi-cairo, gir1.2-gtk-3.0,
 gir1.2-ayatanaappindicator3-0.1 | gir1.2-appindicator3-0.1
Recommends: gnome-shell-extension-appindicator
Homepage: https://github.com/imanimen/tower
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Description: Tower in the menu bar — the top-bar front-end
 The radar in your top bar, and a panel behind it: guard status, network
 weather, every running Claude agent, your location, keep-awake, and plan
 usage. It is the Linux counterpart of Tower's macOS menu-bar app, over the
 same contract — it reads ~/.tower/state.json and writes command files, and
 the daemon in the "tower" package owns all the logic.
 .
 Turning the guard off, or quitting, is warned hard and confirmed twice, and
 the warning says how many agents are working right now and how many chats are
 pinned to the proxy — the same rule both other front-ends follow.
 .
 It draws a StatusNotifierItem, which KDE, XFCE, Cinnamon and Budgie show
 natively. GNOME needs the shipped appindicator extension, hence the
 Recommends; Ubuntu's GNOME session enables it by default.
